{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01WptKsgBCgrCgZKUPHMcWXy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to generate detailed predicted results for each \"planned\" experiment in the experiment_plan, under the \"median\" tier assumptions. Let me carefully go through each planned experiment and generate predictions consistent with the median tier definition.\n\nLet me identify all planned experiments:\n- exp-004: MAVEN confusability study (status: planned in the plan, but there's a registry entry showing it's DONE with conclusion: negative... and another exp004_maven_bcs also DONE. Let me re-read...)\n\nActually, looking more carefully:\n- exp-004 in the experiment_plan says `status: planned`\n- But in the registry, there are entries `exp-004` (DONE, success) and `exp004_maven_bcs` (DONE, negative)\n\n\nSo exp-004 seems to have been partially done. Let me focus on experiments that are truly \"planned\" status in the experiment_plan. Going through the list, I see exp-004 through exp-015 marked as planned, though some like exp-008 have registry entries showing they're already running or completed. I'll include all the ones marked as planned in the plan document and generate predictions for them.\n\nLooking at the experiment_plan, I've identified 12 experiments with planned status. Now I need to work through the median tier predictions for each one, starting with understanding what characterizes the median tier—specifically looking at SDGD-zero ΔF1 values in the [-2, +2] range.\n\nFor the planned experiments, I'm examining what the results would look like if they fall into this median tier. The key is that effects should be directionally consistent but not dramatically large—LLaMA should replicate the pairwise signal on at least one dataset with statistical significance, though possibly with smaller effect sizes than Qwen3. FewRel should confirm the direction with formal results, though variance might prevent all counts from reaching significance. The claims would hold, but Claim 3 would shift from demonstrating clear gains to presenting a principled framework with diagnostic value. For MAVEN, I'd expect the confound analysis and embedding ablation to serve as methodological contributions.\n\nStarting with exp-004 on MAVEN confusability, the registry already shows some baseline metrics—exact F1 is quite low at 0.003-0.035, but relaxed F1 becomes usable at 0.089-0.247, with BCS showing a 2.4x improvement on relaxed F1. low BCS at count_6. For the full study with pairwise, per-type, and count curve analysis, I'm seeing median tier predictions: pairwise MiniLM at r=+0.120, pairwise Qwen3 near -0.007, per-type showing positive direction due to centrality confound, and count curve with F1 increasing alongside count—opposite of Few-NERD because of batch calibration effects.\n\nI notice the registry already has exp-004 and exp004_maven_bcs marked as done, so let me work through what the full analysis would reveal. For MAVEN's confusability study, the count curve with relaxed F1 should show an increasing trend as more types are added, pairwise SCS-confusion with MiniLM around r=0.10-0.13 (p<0.001), Qwen3 staying near zero and non-significant, per-type BCS-F1 correlations positive at ρ=+0.15 to +0.21 driven by the centrality confound, and within-count BCS-relaxed_F1 correlations weak and mixed. For DocRED with 96 relation types, I expect partial replication with noise—pairwise r around 0.06-0.10 with marginal significance, per-type results going in mixed directions.\n\nThe interaction effect test shows additive models fitting better than multiplicative, with the interaction term small and possibly non-significant. The error taxonomy analysis reveals clear separation: high BCS types accumulate more type_substitution errors while low BCS types show more false_negative and boundary errors, supporting the multi-channel model. When I check the LLaMA-3.3-70B results, it replicates the pairwise signal on at least one dataset—Few-NERD pairwise r=0.08-0.12 (p<0.05)—though the effect size is smaller than Qwen3's r=0.156, and per-type results stay directionally consistent.\n\nNow looking at the SDGD-zero experiments: on Few-NERD the median ΔF1 versus single-pass falls in the [-2, +2] percentage point range with no significant improvement, and on MAVEN it's similar with ΔF1 around 0 to +1pp. Adding calibration data in SDGD-cal shows marginal gains—maybe +1-3pp over single-pass on Few-NERD and similar on MAVEN—but these improvements remain marginal. The random batching ablation is starting to come into view. Now I'm compiling the specific numerical ranges for each metric—the F1 deltas across different baselines, the correlation coefficients for the pairwise comparisons, and the extreme value ranges I'm seeing in the confusion matrices and cross-task effects. Let me structure this into the YAML output. I'm working through the MAVEN experiment predictions, noting that the batch-level data already shows the centrality confound paradox where higher BCS correlates with better relaxed F1 scores. For the pairwise analysis with MiniLM, I expect to see a positive correlation around r=+0.120, confirming that more similar pairs tend to get confused more often, and the per-type analysis should show the same positive relationship through the centrality confound lens.\n\nNow I'm ready to structure the full YAML output with the narrative guidance and detailed predictions for the median tier story.\n\nWriting YAML output... 我意识到我已经有足够的上下文来直接生成答案，不需要额外的工具调用——这纯粹是基于提供的信息进行推理和综合。我有所有需要的数据，可以直接写出YAML格式的预测结果。让我仔细处理每个实验的数字，确保为exp-004的MAVEN混淆性研究包含准确的指标值、结果说明和分析细节。\n\n现在我在填充具体的相关性预测：计数曲线显示松弛F1随着计数增加从0.10提升到0.25，这与NER的模式相反；成对相似度指标中MiniLM的相关系数为+0.11（与已知的0.120一致），而Qwen3不显著；按类型分析时两个模型都显示正相关，表明存在中心性混淆因素。\n\n在MAVEN数据集上，168个语义同质的FrameNet类型中，MiniLM能捕捉细粒度的成对语义差异，但Qwen3的嵌入会压缩这些同质类型，导致性能下降；中心类型（语义邻居众多）往往更常见且表现更好，这强化了中心性混淆。转向DocRED的96个关系类型，成对相关性边际显著（r=0.07-0.11），而按类型分析反而出现负相关（ρ=-0.15到-0.20）。\n\n这个数据集跨越多个领域，应该更接近Few-NERD的特性，但文档级关系抽取本身噪声更大，关系类型的语义也更复杂，所以效应量被衰减了。现在我在检查一个2×2的交互效应设计，对比低/高样本数和低/高BCS的组合，发现样本数的主效应显著（F1下降约8个百分点），BCS的主效应也显著（下降约5个百分点），但两者的交互效应很小且不显著。\n\n两个模型的拟合度都在0.35-0.36之间，这说明在中位数层级上两个因素各自独立发挥作用。交互效应弱的原因是样本数影响召回率（遗漏错误），而BCS影响精确率（替换错误），它们作用在不同的错误类型上。现在我在分析错误分类的分布，预期高BCS的情况下类型替换错误占60-70%，而低BCS时这个比例会降到25-35%，类型替换的比率大约是2-2.5倍。\n\n遗漏率随样本数单调增加，替换率则同时受样本数和BCS影响。这个模式支持多通道模型的假设——高BCS导致类型混淆（跨度正确但标签错误），而低BCS加高样本数导致实体遗漏（注意力分散）。现在用LLaMA-3.3-70B验证这个模式，相关性系数比Qwen3小得多（0.09 vs 0.156），但混淆率的极端比例达到6-15倍，召回率曲线形状相似。\n\n我预期LLaMA在NER任务上整体表现会弱5-10%，因为它处理提示的方式不同，但关键是要在至少一个数据集上看到r≥0.08且p<0.05的显著信号。同时在Few-NERD上测试SDGD-zero方法，预期在count_64等效条件下F1达到0.42-0.44，与单轮传递的0.41-0.43相当。\n\nSDGD-zero相比单轮传递的改进很小（+0.5到+1.5个百分点），统计上不显著，但它通过将易混淆的类型分离到不同批次来减少类型混淆错误（降低15-25%），代价是失去跨类型上下文导致遗漏增加。虽然总体F1变化不大，但错误分布发生了转变——替换错误减少，遗漏错误增加——这支持了框架的有效性。\n\n在MAVEN数据集上，由于其类型空间高度同质化，SDGD-zero的改进更加有限，因为即使是低混淆性批次仍然具有中等程度的相似性，高基础相似度限制了该方法的效果。\n\n对于Few-NERD上的SDGD-cal，使用实际的模型混淆数据而非嵌入代理能捕捉到更真实的混淆模式，相比SDGD-zero有1-2.5个百分点的改进，但由于Few-NERD的66个类型构成中等复杂度的模式，经验混淆数据的收集成本约为330-660次API调用，而改进幅度仍然相对温和。\n\n在MAVEN上，这种方法的优势更明显，因为嵌入代理在同质模式上表现不佳，而经验混淆数据能更好地反映实际模型行为。现在看随机批处理的消融实验，预期F1在0.42-0.44之间。\n\n随机批处理通过减少每批数量（从66降到约11）来改进，这提供了一些收益，但SDGD-zero通过混淆感知分组获得的额外收益在中位数层级上相对较小，因为混淆度降低被上下文损失部分抵消了。关键发现是计数减少和混淆度减少两个因素贡献大致相当，但都很有限。接下来是按类型分割的实验，预期F1在0.38-0.42之间。\n\n按类型分割虽然完全消除了类型混淆，但也失去了所有跨类型上下文——对于Few-NERD这样有相关类型的复杂模式，模型无法区分类型，因为它们从不一起出现，这种\"消歧上下文损失\"的伤害超过了混淆度降低的帮助，同时高延迟使其不切实际，这个结果反而强化了SDGD作为平衡方案的价值。\n\n现在看SCS验证的结果，嵌入相似度与实际混淆的相关性是中等的——Spearman相关系数在0.28-0.38之间，这说明SCS是合理但不完美的代理，因为实际混淆还依赖于模型特定因素如类型名称的词汇重叠和预训练频率，而SCS只捕捉了可混淆性的一个维度。这个中等相关性支持SDGD-zero作为合理近似，同时也说明SDGD-cal能提供更高质量的结果。\n\n现在需要准备完整的YAML输出，但先要核实几个关键对比：exp-008应该是count_64的单轮传递基线对比SDGD-zero的多批次分割，而V2提示在count_64上的F1是0.414，SDGD-zero需要超过这个基线。\n\n对于中位数层级，SDGD-zero可能达到F1=0.41-0.43，相比单轮传递的0.414，差值在-0.5到+1.5个百分点之间，这样更诚实地反映了不确定性。同时还要考虑SDGD相比随机批处理的表现差异，范围在[-1, 2]个百分点。\n\n现在我需要整理这些预测并生成YAML格式的结果。\n\n等等，我需要重新理解用户的需求——他们要求对实验计划中每个标记为planned的实验提供详细数据预测。虽然exp-004和fewrel_pilot在注册表中已有真实数据，但我应该针对计划中的实验进行预测，同时在相关处承认现有数据的存在。\n\n对于exp-004到exp-015这些planned状态的实验，我需要逐一预测完整的分析结果。对于exp-008虽然注册表显示失败和运行中，但我应该预测成功运行的预期结果。我还需要检查实验计划中是否有特定的\"fewrel formal\"实验ID，因为目前只看到fewrel_pilot在注册表中。\n\n根据论文框架中的证据层级，FewRel formal似乎是一个子分析而非独立实验，所以我不会单独列出它。现在开始系统地组织YAML输出，按实验ID逐个处理，并为每个实验包含相关的关键表格。\n\n对于exp-004，描述提到\"计数曲线加MAVEN事件检测中的计数内BCS相关性\"，注册表中已有计数曲线数据和一些BCS控制数据，但论文框架中标记为完成的是完整的成对分析和按类型分析（MiniLM成对r=0.120），所以exp-004可能已经完成了，我来预测完整结果并开始生成综合YAML。","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":17842,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":17842},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ae22442b-8538-43ef-9b60-9e46bd12db0d","uuid":"af2dfb50-bea3-462e-8722-f2d3bc2cec30"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01WptKsgBCgrCgZKUPHMcWXy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: median\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  论文重心 80:20（分析:方法）。三层贡献：(1) pairwise confusability 跨 NER/RE/ED 三任务、Qwen3+LLaMA 双模型成立，\n  (2) multi-channel degradation model（count→omission, confusability→substitution）+ 错误分类学，\n  (3) centrality confound 方法论发现 + 2×3 embedding ablation practitioner guidance。\n  SDGD-zero 保留为 proof-of-concept 但 ΔF1 不显著（[-2,+2]pp），Claim 3 改写为\n  \"SDGD 框架示范 pairwise confusability 可直接指导 schema decomposition，SDGD-cal 预期有更大空间\"。\n  EMNLP Main 可冲（对标 Lost in the Middle），Findings 作后备。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"MAVEN Full Confusability Study\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-004\"\n    description: >\n      MAVEN 168 event类型，count curve + within-count BCS correlation + pairwise/per-type分析。\n      跨任务验证（NER→ED），同域语义密集 schema 的 confusability 行为。\n    expected_results:\n      count_curve_relaxed_f1:\n        count_1: 0.106\n        count_6: 0.103\n        count_12: 0.146\n        count_22: 0.185\n        count_44: 0.247\n        count_64: 0.245\n        count_168: 0.220\n      count_curve_exact_f1:\n        count_1: 0.009\n        count_6: 0.003\n        count_12: 0.008\n        count_22: 0.013\n        count_44: 0.018\n        count_64: 0.013\n      pairwise_minilm:\n        pearson_r: 0.115\n        pearson_p: 2.0e-34\n        n_pairs: 11026\n        spearman_rho: 0.098\n        spearman_p: 1.5e-24\n      pairwise_qwen3:\n        pearson_r: -0.007\n        pearson_p: 0.41\n        verdict: \"NOT_SIGNIFICANT\"\n      per_type_qwen3:\n        spearman_rho: 0.189\n        spearman_p: 0.021\n        direction: \"POSITIVE (centrality confound)\"\n      per_type_minilm:\n        spearman_rho: 0.208\n        spearman_p: 0.011\n        direction: \"POSITIVE (centrality confound)\"\n      within_count_bcs_relaxed_f1:\n        count_6_r: 0.12\n        count_6_p: 0.18\n        count_12_r: 0.09\n        count_12_p: 0.28\n        verdict: \"FAIL — batch-level BCS confounded by centrality\"\n      confusion_rate_ratio_extreme:\n        count_6: 7.5\n        count_12: 5.2\n    result_rationale: >\n      MAVEN 168 类型全部来自 FrameNet 同域层级，语义空间高度同质（scs_mean=0.216，\n      scs_std=0.103），导致两个层面行为分离：\n      (1) Pairwise MiniLM 成立（r≈0.12）——因为 MiniLM 对细粒度事件类型对（如 Destroying↔Damaging）\n      的相对差异敏感，pair-level 分析不受聚合效应影响；\n      (2) Pairwise Qwen3 不显著——Qwen3 extraction-aligned embedding 在同域 schema 中\n      将语义相近类型压缩到近乎相同的向量，丧失区分力；\n      (3) Per-type 两种 embedding 均为正向 ρ≈+0.19/+0.21——这是 centrality confound：\n      在同质 schema 中 mean BCS 高的类型恰好是语义中心、高频类型，LLM 对其提取效果好。\n      这不是分析失败，而是方法论贡献——识别出\"per-type 聚合在何时失效\"的具体机制。\n      Within-count batch-level 相关不显著，因为 batch-level BCS 范围被 schema 同质性压缩\n      （0.87-0.94），区分度不足。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: MAVEN Count Curve (Relaxed F1)\"\n        content: |\n          | Count | Relaxed F1 | Exact F1 | Recall | Precision |\n          |-------|-----------|----------|--------|-----------|\n          | 1     | 0.106     | 0.009    | 0.142  | 0.083     |\n          | 6     | 0.103     | 0.003    | 0.130  | 0.085     |\n          | 12    | 0.146     | 0.008    | 0.172  | 0.127     |\n          | 22    | 0.185     | 0.013    | 0.210  | 0.165     |\n          | 44    | 0.247     | 0.018    | 0.268  | 0.229     |\n          | 64    | 0.245     | 0.013    | 0.255  | 0.236     |\n      - name: \"Table: MAVEN Pairwise & Per-type Analysis (2×2 Embedding Matrix)\"\n        content: |\n          | Level     | Qwen3          | MiniLM          |\n          |-----------|----------------|-----------------|\n          | Pairwise  | r=-0.007 (ns)  | r=+0.115 ✓      |\n          | Per-type  | ρ=+0.189 ✗     | ρ=+0.208 ✗      |\n          Note: ✓=supports confusability hypothesis, ✗=centrality confound direction\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scatter plot: MiniLM pairwise SCS vs confusion count (11K pairs), with regression line r=0.115. Long tail of high-SCS pairs with elevated confusion.\"\n      - \"Bar chart: per-type mean BCS quartiles vs relaxed F1, showing positive trend (centrality confound). Annotated with frequency distribution per quartile.\"\n      - \"Heatmap: top-20 confused event type pairs, colored by MiniLM SCS. Diagonal stripe pattern showing FrameNet siblings.\"\n    analysis: >\n      MAVEN 为 pairwise confusability 提供跨任务复现（NER→ED），同时暴露 per-type 聚合的\n      centrality confound 机制。MiniLM pairwise r=0.115 与 Few-NERD r=0.156 量级一致，\n      但 Qwen3 在同域 schema 上失效，证实\"embedding 选择影响信号检测\"的结论。\n      Per-type 正向 ρ 构成独立方法论贡献：当 schema 语义同质时，mean BCS 不再是\n      confusability 的有效聚合指标，需回退到 pairwise level。\n\n  - name: \"DocRED Confusability Scaling Test\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-005\"\n    description: >\n      DocRED 96 relation types，count curve + BCS correlation。\n      文档级 RE 的 scaling stress test，验证 confusability 信号在更复杂抽取设置下是否成立。\n    expected_results:\n      count_curve_f1:\n        count_1: 0.18\n        count_6: 0.22\n        count_12: 0.25\n        count_24: 0.23\n        count_48: 0.19\n        count_96: 0.14\n      pairwise_qwen3:\n        pearson_r: 0.082\n        pearson_p: 0.008\n        n_pairs: 4560\n      pairwise_minilm:\n        pearson_r: 0.095\n        pearson_p: 0.001\n      per_type_qwen3:\n        spearman_rho: -0.165\n        spearman_p: 0.108\n      within_count_bcs_f1:\n        count_12_r: 0.18\n        count_12_p: 0.12\n        count_24_r: 0.25\n        count_24_p: 0.065\n    result_rationale: >\n      DocRED 是文档级 RE，96 relation types 跨越多域（人物、地理、组织等），\n      语义异质性介于 Few-NERD（跨域 NER）和 MAVEN（同域 ED）之间。\n      Pairwise 信号可检测（r≈0.08-0.10）但弱于 Few-NERD（r=0.156），原因是：\n      (1) 文档级 RE 噪声更大——同一文档多个 relation 共现，confusion 来源更复杂；\n      (2) relation type 的语义相似性比 entity type 更抽象（\"country of citizenship\" vs\n      \"place of birth\" 的 embedding 距离不完全反映 LLM 的实际混淆模式）；\n      (3) DocRED 的 distant supervision 标注本身有噪声，增加 metric variance。\n      Per-type 方向一致（负 ρ）但因 n=96 types + 噪声，未达显著。\n      作为 P1 实验，主要贡献是\"第四个数据点\"但非必须——三任务已足够。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: DocRED Count Curve\"\n        content: |\n          | Count | F1    | Recall | Precision |\n          |-------|-------|--------|-----------|\n          | 1     | 0.180 | 0.280  | 0.133     |\n          | 6     | 0.220 | 0.290  | 0.178     |\n          | 12    | 0.250 | 0.275  | 0.229     |\n          | 24    | 0.230 | 0.240  | 0.221     |\n          | 48    | 0.190 | 0.195  | 0.185     |\n          | 96    | 0.140 | 0.135  | 0.146     |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"DocRED count curve overlay with Few-NERD (normalized F1), showing both exhibit inverted-U but DocRED peaks earlier (count_12 vs count_44).\"\n    analysis: >\n      DocRED 提供第四个数据点但效应量衰减。如果时间紧张（ARR deadline 10 天），\n      可降级为 appendix 或完全跳过——Few-NERD + FewRel + MAVEN 已覆盖 NER/RE/ED 三任务。\n\n  - name: \"Count × Confusability Interaction Effect\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-006\"\n    description: >\n      2×2 factorial：{low count (6), high count (22)} × {low BCS, high BCS}，Few-NERD。\n      检验 count 和 confusability 的交互是加性还是乘性。\n    expected_results:\n      cell_f1:\n        low_count_low_bcs: 0.355\n        low_count_high_bcs: 0.305\n        high_count_low_bcs: 0.295\n        high_count_high_bcs: 0.230\n      main_effect_count:\n        delta_f1_pp: -6.3\n        f_stat: 8.2\n        p_value: 0.007\n      main_effect_bcs:\n        delta_f1_pp: -5.8\n        f_stat: 6.5\n        p_value: 0.015\n      interaction:\n        f_stat: 1.4\n        p_value: 0.24\n        effect_size_eta2: 0.03\n      model_comparison:\n        additive_R2: 0.38\n        multiplicative_R2: 0.39\n    result_rationale: >\n      Count 和 confusability 通过不同通道降解性能：count 导致 recall 下降（omission），\n      confusability 导致 precision 下降（substitution）。这两个通道大致正交——\n      增加 count 不会显著放大 confusability 的效应，反之亦然。\n      Interaction term 不显著（p≈0.24）的原因是：(1) 两通道作用于不同错误类型，\n      物理上近似独立；(2) 2×2 设计只有 ~20 batches/cell，检测交互效应的统计功效有限。\n      Additive model 已解释 ~38% 方差，interaction 仅贡献 1%。\n      这实际上支持 multi-channel model 的核心主张——count 和 confusability 可独立处理。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: 2×2 Factorial Results\"\n        content: |\n          |                | Low BCS  | High BCS | Marginal |\n          |----------------|----------|----------|----------|\n          | Low count (6)  | 0.355    | 0.305    | 0.330    |\n          | High count (22)| 0.295    | 0.230    | 0.263    |\n          | Marginal       | 0.325    | 0.268    |          |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Interaction plot: two roughly parallel lines (low BCS, high BCS) across count levels, illustrating additive (not synergistic) effect.\"\n    analysis: >\n      加性模型优于乘性模型但 margin 很小。关键 takeaway 是\"two independent knobs\"——\n      从业者可以分别优化 batch size（控制 count 通道）和 batch composition（控制 confusability 通道），\n      无需考虑复杂交互。这是 practitioner guidance 的基础。\n\n  - name: \"Systematic Error Taxonomy\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-007\"\n    description: >\n      跨 BCS bins 的 FP 系统分类：type_substitution / boundary_error / omission / hallucination。\n      为 multi-channel model 提供机制证据。\n    expected_results:\n      error_distribution_high_bcs:\n        type_substitution_pct: 62\n        boundary_error_pct: 14\n        omission_pct: 18\n        hallucination_pct: 6\n      error_distribution_low_bcs:\n        type_substitution_pct: 28\n        boundary_error_pct: 22\n        omission_pct: 42\n        hallucination_pct: 8\n      error_distribution_medium_bcs:\n        type_substitution_pct: 45\n        boundary_error_pct: 18\n        omission_pct: 30\n        hallucination_pct: 7\n      substitution_ratio_high_vs_low: 2.2\n      omission_ratio_low_vs_high: 2.3\n      substitution_trend_with_count:\n        count_6: 0.35\n        count_12: 0.48\n        count_22: 0.55\n      omission_trend_with_count:\n        count_6: 0.28\n        count_12: 0.32\n        count_22: 0.38\n    result_rationale: >\n      Error taxonomy 是 multi-channel model 的直接机制验证。\n      High-BCS batches 中 type_substitution 占主导（~62%）因为语义相似类型共现时\n      LLM 识别了正确的 span 但选错了类型标签——这正是 confusability channel 的定义。\n      Low-BCS batches 中 omission 占主导（~42%）因为虽然类型不相似但数量多，\n      LLM 的 attention 被分散，更多实体被完全遗漏——这是 count channel。\n      Substitution 随 count 增加（0.35→0.55）因为更多类型意味着更多潜在混淆对。\n      Omission 也随 count 增加（0.28→0.38）因为 attention dilution 加剧。\n      两种错误都对 count 有响应，但 confusability 只放大 substitution，不影响 omission——\n      这是两通道正交性的直接证据。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Error Distribution by BCS Bin\"\n        content: |\n          | Error Type       | Low BCS | Med BCS | High BCS |\n          |------------------|---------|---------|----------|\n          | Type Substitution| 28%     | 45%     | 62%      |\n          | Boundary Error   | 22%     | 18%     | 14%      |\n          | Omission         | 42%     | 30%     | 18%      |\n          | Hallucination    | 8%      | 7%      | 6%       |\n      - name: \"Table: Error Rates by Count Level (All BCS)\"\n        content: |\n          | Error Type       | Count 6 | Count 12 | Count 22 |\n          |------------------|---------|----------|----------|\n          | Substitution Rate| 0.035   | 0.048    | 0.055    |\n          | Omission Rate    | 0.028   | 0.032    | 0.038    |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Stacked bar chart: error type composition across 5 BCS quintiles, showing substitution/omission crossover at BCS≈0.82.\"\n      - \"Dual-axis line chart: substitution rate (left axis) and omission rate (right axis) vs count, both increasing but substitution steeper.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Error taxonomy 将 \"confusability degrades extraction\" 的抽象主张具象化为可操作的诊断框架：\n      看到 high substitution rate → confusability 问题 → SDGD-style decomposition；\n      看到 high omission rate → count 问题 → reduce batch size。\n      这本身是论文的独立贡献，特别是在 Claim 3 (SDGD gains) 不显著的 median 档下，\n      错误分类学提供了\"分析即贡献\"的具体证据。\n\n  - name: \"LLaMA-3.3-70B Multi-Model Validation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-012\"\n    description: >\n      LLaMA-3.3-70B-Instruct 复现 exp-002 协议。\n      验证 confusability 信号的模型无关性——是 schema 属性而非模型特异行为。\n    expected_results:\n      fewnerd_pairwise:\n        pearson_r: 0.098\n        pearson_p: 3.2e-05\n        n_pairs: 1953\n        spearman_rho: 0.105\n        spearman_p: 8.7e-06\n        nonzero_spearman_rho: 0.195\n        nonzero_spearman_p: 0.0004\n      fewnerd_per_type:\n        spearman_rho: -0.215\n        spearman_p: 0.089\n        partial_r_ctrl_logfreq: -0.155\n        partial_p: 0.225\n      count_curve_f1:\n        count_1: 0.285\n        count_6: 0.270\n        count_12: 0.305\n        count_22: 0.265\n        count_44: 0.380\n        count_64: 0.355\n      confusion_rate_ratio_extreme:\n        count_6: 12.5\n        count_12: 6.8\n      batch_level_f1_vs_bcs:\n        count_12_r: 0.38\n        count_12_p: 0.045\n    result_rationale: >\n      LLaMA-3.3-70B 复现 pairwise 信号（r≈0.10, p<0.001）但效应量小于 Qwen3（r=0.156），\n      原因是：\n      (1) LLaMA 和 Qwen3 架构不同（LLaMA 使用 GQA vs Qwen3 使用 GQA+SWA），\n      对 prompt 中类型列表的 attention 分配模式不同，导致 confusability 的表现形式有差异；\n      (2) LLaMA-70B 参数量更大（70B vs 32B），可能对 confusable types 有更强的区分能力，\n      从而压缩效应量；\n      (3) 但 pairwise 信号方向一致且显著——confusability 是 schema 结构属性，\n      不同模型都会受影响，只是程度不同。\n      Per-type ρ=-0.215 方向一致但 p=0.089 未达 0.05——这在 median 档预期范围内\n      （cross_model_significant: [1,2]），pairwise 显著已足够支撑 multi-model claim。\n      Overall F1 水平比 Qwen3 低 5-10%，可能因 LLaMA 的 NER few-shot 能力略弱。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Cross-Model Pairwise Comparison\"\n        content: |\n          | Metric              | Qwen3-32B   | LLaMA-3.3-70B |\n          |---------------------|-------------|---------------|\n          | Pairwise r          | 0.156       | 0.098         |\n          | Pairwise p          | 4.6e-12     | 3.2e-05       |\n          | Per-type ρ          | -0.293*     | -0.215        |\n          | Confusion ratio (6) | 27.5x       | 12.5x         |\n          | Confusion ratio (12)| 9.9x        | 6.8x          |\n          * p<0.05\n      - name: \"Table: LLaMA Count Curve\"\n        content: |\n          | Count | F1    | Recall | Precision |\n          |-------|-------|--------|-----------|\n          | 1     | 0.285 | 0.580  | 0.190     |\n          | 6     | 0.270 | 0.420  | 0.200     |\n          | 12    | 0.305 | 0.310  | 0.300     |\n          | 22    | 0.265 | 0.255  | 0.275     |\n          | 44    | 0.380 | 0.365  | 0.396     |\n          | 64    | 0.355 | 0.280  | 0.485     |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Overlay scatter: Qwen3 vs LLaMA pairwise SCS-confusion, same axes. Both positive slopes, LLaMA shallower.\"\n      - \"Side-by-side confusion heatmaps (top-20 pairs): substantial overlap in confused pairs between models.\"\n    analysis: >\n      LLaMA 在 pairwise level 显著复现信号（r≥0.08, p<0.05），满足 median 档\n      cross_model_significant ≥1 的阈值。Per-type 未达显著但方向一致。\n      效应量差异本身是有意义的发现——更大的模型可能对 confusability 更鲁棒，\n      暗示 confusability 降解是 training-free setting 的固有挑战，可通过 scaling 部分缓解但不消除。\n      论文中报告为\"cross-model replication with attenuated but significant effect\"。\n\n  - name: \"SDGD-zero on Few-NERD\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-008\"\n    description: >\n      Confusability-minimizing batch composition：embedding SCS 阈值化 → confusability graph →\n      graph coloring → batches。对比 single-pass full-schema baseline。\n    expected_results:\n      sdgd_zero_config:\n        embedding: \"qwen3\"\n        threshold: 0.85\n        n_batches: 8\n        avg_batch_size: 8.25\n        coloring_algorithm: \"greedy_dsatur\"\n      sdgd_zero_f1: 0.425\n      singlepass_f1: 0.414\n      delta_f1_pp: 1.1\n      delta_f1_ci_95: [-1.5, 3.7]\n      p_value_paired_t: 0.18\n      significant: false\n      sdgd_zero_recall: 0.335\n      sdgd_zero_precision: 0.580\n      singlepass_recall: 0.304\n      singlepass_precision: 0.648\n      type_confusion_errors:\n        sdgd_zero: 1850\n        singlepass: 2434\n        reduction_pct: 24\n      omission_errors:\n        sdgd_zero: 3200\n        singlepass: 2850\n        increase_pct: 12\n      api_calls: 8\n      wall_clock_ratio: 3.2\n    result_rationale: >\n      SDGD-zero 在 median 档下 ΔF1≈+1.1pp，置信区间跨零，不显著。核心权衡：\n      (1) Confusability 降低的收益——分离 confusable types（如 person-other 和 person-politician\n      不再共现于同一 batch），type confusion errors 减少 ~24%，precision 改善；\n      (2) 跨类型上下文丢失的代价——单 batch 只看到 ~8 个类型而非全部 66 个，\n      LLM 无法利用\"这不是 X 所以应该是 Y\"的排除推理，omission errors 增加 ~12%；\n      (3) 这两个效应在 F1 层面大致抵消。Precision 提升（0.648→0.580 actually下降...\n      不对，让我修正）——SDGD-zero 的 recall 高于 single-pass（0.335>0.304）因为\n      smaller batches 意味着更少的 attention dilution，但 precision 降低因为\n      smaller batches 使模型缺少同 batch 内的对比信号。\n      净效应：recall 提升 + precision 下降 → F1 微小提升但不显著。\n      这正是 median 档的核心判断——decomposition 是可行的框架但不是 silver bullet。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: SDGD-zero vs Single-pass on Few-NERD (66 types)\"\n        content: |\n          | Method      | F1    | Recall | Precision | Type Confusion | Omission | API Calls |\n          |-------------|-------|--------|-----------|----------------|----------|-----------|\n          | Single-pass | 0.414 | 0.304  | 0.648     | 2434           | 2850     | 1         |\n          | SDGD-zero   | 0.425 | 0.335  | 0.580     | 1850           | 3200     | 8         |\n          | Δ           | +1.1  | +3.1   | -6.8      | -24%           | +12%     | +7        |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Paired bar chart: error type breakdown for single-pass vs SDGD-zero, showing substitution↓ / omission↑ tradeoff.\"\n      - \"Scatter: per-batch F1 vs batch mean BCS for SDGD-zero batches, showing SDGD batches cluster at low BCS.\"\n    analysis: >\n      SDGD-zero 的价值不在于 F1 增益（不显著），而在于：\n      (1) 验证 pairwise confusability 可直接转化为 actionable decomposition；\n      (2) 错误 profile 的定向转移证实 multi-channel model——confusability channel 可关闭（减 24% substitution），\n      但代价是轻度激活 count channel（增 12% omission）；\n      (3) 为 SDGD-cal 提供 baseline——如果用 empirical confusion 替代 embedding proxy，\n      graph 更准确，预期收益更大。\n\n  - name: \"SDGD-zero on MAVEN\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-009\"\n    description: >\n      SDGD-zero 在 MAVEN 168 event types 上的跨任务验证。\n      同域高密度 schema 对 graph coloring 的挑战。\n    expected_results:\n      sdgd_zero_config:\n        embedding: \"minilm\"\n        threshold: 0.35\n        n_batches: 14\n        avg_batch_size: 12\n      sdgd_zero_relaxed_f1: 0.240\n      singlepass_relaxed_f1: 0.245\n      random_batching_relaxed_f1: 0.235\n      delta_vs_singlepass_pp: -0.5\n      delta_vs_random_pp: 0.5\n      significant: false\n      sdgd_zero_exact_f1: 0.015\n      singlepass_exact_f1: 0.013\n      api_calls: 14\n    result_rationale: >\n      MAVEN 的同域同质 schema 对 SDGD-zero 极具挑战：\n      (1) SCS 分布集中（mean=0.216, std=0.103），大部分 pair 相似度在 0.1-0.35 范围，\n      用阈值 0.35 切分后 confusability graph 边数较少，graph coloring 产生的 batches\n      与 random batching 差异不大；\n      (2) 即使成功分离了高 SCS pairs（119 pairs > 0.5），这些 pairs 分布在 168 个 types\n      中仅占 0.85%，对整体 F1 影响微小；\n      (3) Exact F1 极低（<0.02）使得任何方法差异都淹没在 boundary matching 噪声中，\n      relaxed F1 是唯一可比指标；\n      (4) SDGD-zero 微弱优于 random batching（+0.5pp），但不优于 single-pass（-0.5pp），\n      因为 MAVEN 的 context 更重要——event detection 依赖同一句中多种事件类型的对比。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: SDGD-zero vs Baselines on MAVEN (168 types)\"\n        content: |\n          | Method          | Relaxed F1 | Exact F1 | API Calls |\n          |-----------------|-----------|----------|-----------|\n          | Single-pass     | 0.245     | 0.013    | 1         |\n          | Random (k=14)   | 0.235     | 0.012    | 14        |\n          | SDGD-zero       | 0.240     | 0.015    | 14        |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"MAVEN confusability graph visualization: near-complete subgraph structure, illustrating why graph coloring fails to find clean separations.\"\n    analysis: >\n      MAVEN 上 SDGD-zero ≈ single-pass 进一步支持 median 档叙事：\n      SDGD 是正确的框架但 -zero 变体在高密度 schema 上能力有限。\n      这也解释了为什么 embedding-based proxy 不够——需要 empirical confusion data (SDGD-cal)\n      才能在同域 schema 上有效操作。\n\n  - name: \"SDGD-cal on Few-NERD\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-010\"\n    description: >\n      用 5-10 calibration examples 的 empirical confusion matrix 替代 embedding SCS 构建 confusability graph。\n      检验 calibration 数据能否弥补 embedding proxy 的不足。\n    expected_results:\n      calibration_config:\n        n_calibration_examples: 8\n        calibration_api_calls: 528\n        total_api_calls: 536\n      sdgd_cal_f1: 0.440\n      sdgd_zero_f1: 0.425\n      singlepass_f1: 0.414\n      delta_cal_vs_zero_pp: 1.5\n      delta_cal_vs_singlepass_pp: 2.6\n      delta_cal_vs_singlepass_ci_95: [-0.8, 6.0]\n      p_value_vs_singlepass: 0.09\n      significant_vs_singlepass: false\n      type_confusion_reduction_vs_singlepass_pct: 35\n      calibration_confusion_vs_scs_spearman: 0.32\n    result_rationale: >\n      SDGD-cal 相比 SDGD-zero 提升 ~1.5pp，原因是 empirical confusion 直接捕获\n      模型特异的混淆模式（如 Qwen3 特别容易混淆 building-library ↔ building-hotel\n      但 embedding 距离中等的 pair），绕过了 embedding proxy 的噪声。\n      但 +2.6pp vs single-pass 仍不显著（p≈0.09），因为：\n      (1) 8 个 calibration examples 的 confusion matrix 高方差——很多 type pairs\n      在 8 个样本中从未共现，confusion 为 0 但真实 confusability 非零；\n      (2) 从 calibration 到 test set 的 confusion 分布偏移——calibration examples\n      的 type 分布未必代表 test set；\n      (3) context loss 问题仍在——SDGD-cal 只改善了 confusability graph 的质量，\n      不改变 decomposition 本身的 context-loss tradeoff。\n      这个结果在 median 档下留出\"SDGD-cal 有空间\"的 narrative——\n      更多 calibration data 或更好的 calibration protocol 预期可以继续提升。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: SDGD Variant Comparison on Few-NERD\"\n        content: |\n          | Method      | F1    | ΔF1 vs SP | Type Confusion ↓ | API Calls |\n          |-------------|-------|-----------|------------------|-----------|\n          | Single-pass | 0.414 | —         | —                | 1         |\n          | SDGD-zero   | 0.425 | +1.1      | -24%             | 8         |\n          | SDGD-cal    | 0.440 | +2.6      | -35%             | 536       |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Line chart: F1 improvement trajectory from single-pass → SDGD-zero → SDGD-cal, with error bars. Upward trend but CIs overlap.\"\n      - \"Confusion matrix diff: empirical (calibration) vs embedding-predicted, highlighting discrepancies.\"\n    analysis: >\n      SDGD-cal 展示 confusability-aware decomposition 的 ceiling 更高，\n      但 8-example calibration 尚不足以稳定地达到。论文可报告为\"SDGD-cal 提供方向，\n      充分 calibration 数据下预期更大收益，但当前 training-free 设定下的 calibration 成本\n      与收益比尚需优化\"。作为 SDGD-cal 的存在证明而非 headline 结果。\n\n  - name: \"SDGD-cal on MAVEN\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-011\"\n    description: >\n      SDGD-cal 在 MAVEN 168 event types 上运行。\n      测试 empirical confusion 能否克服 MAVEN 上 embedding proxy 失效的问题。\n    expected_results:\n      sdgd_cal_relaxed_f1: 0.258\n      sdgd_zero_relaxed_f1: 0.240\n      singlepass_relaxed_f1: 0.245\n      delta_cal_vs_singlepass_pp: 1.3\n      delta_cal_vs_zero_pp: 1.8\n      significant: false\n      calibration_api_calls: 1344\n      total_api_calls: 1358\n    result_rationale: >\n      MAVEN 上 SDGD-cal 比 SDGD-zero 收益更大（+1.8pp vs +0.5pp on Few-NERD），\n      因为 MAVEN 正是 embedding proxy 失效的数据集（Qwen3 pairwise r=-0.007）。\n      Empirical confusion 绕过了 embedding 的限制，直接用模型行为构建 graph。\n      但绝对增益仍有限（+1.3pp vs single-pass），因为：\n      (1) 168 types 的 calibration matrix 极其稀疏——168×167/2=14028 pairs 中，\n      8 个 calibration samples 能覆盖的 pair 比例很低；\n      (2) MAVEN 的 exact F1 极低，relaxed F1 的 variance 大，信噪比低；\n      (3) 1344 API calls 的 calibration 成本在实用性上存疑。\n      这支持了\"SDGD-cal 在 embedding 失效场景下价值更大\"的论点，\n      也说明了\"calibration 效率是未来工作方向\"。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: SDGD-cal vs Baselines on MAVEN\"\n        content: |\n          | Method      | Relaxed F1 | Δ vs SP  | API Calls |\n          |-------------|-----------|----------|-----------|\n          | Single-pass | 0.245     | —        | 1         |\n          | SDGD-zero   | 0.240     | -0.5     | 14        |\n          | SDGD-cal    | 0.258     | +1.3     | 1358      |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Grouped bar chart: SDGD-zero vs SDGD-cal improvement over single-pass, Few-NERD vs MAVEN. MAVEN shows larger cal-zero gap.\"\n    analysis: >\n      MAVEN 上 SDGD-cal > SDGD-zero 的差距（1.8pp）大于 Few-NERD（1.5pp），\n      验证了\"当 embedding proxy 失效时 empirical calibration 价值更高\"的预测。\n      但绝对增益仍不显著，reinforces median-tier narrative。\n\n  - name: \"Random Batching Ablation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-013\"\n    description: >\n      Random batching（与 SDGD 同 k，随机分组）ablation。\n      隔离 confusability-aware grouping 的贡献 vs 纯 batch count reduction。\n    expected_results:\n      random_batching_f1: 0.418\n      sdgd_zero_f1: 0.425\n      singlepass_f1: 0.414\n      delta_sdgd_vs_random_pp: 0.7\n      delta_random_vs_singlepass_pp: 0.4\n      random_batching_recall: 0.325\n      random_batching_precision: 0.565\n      type_confusion_errors:\n        random: 2150\n        sdgd_zero: 1850\n        singlepass: 2434\n      n_random_seeds: 5\n      f1_std_across_seeds: 0.018\n    result_rationale: >\n      Random batching vs single-pass 仅 +0.4pp——count reduction 本身的收益很小，\n      因为 Few-NERD 66 types 分成 8 batches of ~8 types，每个 batch 仍然有足够的\n      type diversity 来产生 confusion。Random batching 的 confusion rate 高于 SDGD-zero\n      但低于 single-pass，因为随机分组偶然也会分开一些 confusable pairs。\n      SDGD-zero vs random 的差异（+0.7pp）代表了 confusability-aware grouping 的\n      增量贡献——统计上不显著但方向一致，5 seeds 的 F1 std=0.018 反映分组方案敏感性。\n      这个结果在 median 档下支持\"SDGD 的 confusability-aware grouping 有正面方向\n      但需要更好的 confusability 信号（如 SDGD-cal）才能变得显著\"的叙事。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Batching Strategy Ablation (Few-NERD, k=8)\"\n        content: |\n          | Strategy     | F1    | Recall | Prec  | TypeConfusion | Seeds |\n          |-------------|-------|--------|-------|---------------|-------|\n          | Single-pass | 0.414 | 0.304  | 0.648 | 2434          | 1     |\n          | Random      | 0.418 | 0.325  | 0.565 | 2150          | 5     |\n          | SDGD-zero   | 0.425 | 0.335  | 0.580 | 1850          | 1     |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Box plot: 5 random seeds' F1 distribution vs SDGD-zero (single point), SDGD-zero at or near upper end of random distribution.\"\n    analysis: >\n      SDGD-zero 位于 random batching 分布的上端但未显著超出——\n      这意味着 confusability-aware grouping 有 signal 但 magnitude 有限。\n      报告为\"SDGD directionality confirmed, magnitude requires stronger confusability signal\"。\n\n  - name: \"Per-type Splitting (UniNER-style) Ablation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-014\"\n    description: >\n      每个 type 一个 batch（k=66），UniNER 风格。\n      消融 decomposition 的上界和 cross-type context loss 效应。\n    expected_results:\n      per_type_f1: 0.395\n      sdgd_zero_f1: 0.425\n      singlepass_f1: 0.414\n      delta_per_type_vs_singlepass_pp: -1.9\n      delta_per_type_vs_sdgd_pp: -3.0\n      per_type_recall: 0.385\n      per_type_precision: 0.405\n      api_calls: 66\n      wall_clock_minutes: 45\n      sdgd_wall_clock_minutes: 12\n      singlepass_wall_clock_minutes: 4\n      type_confusion_errors: 0\n      omission_errors: 4500\n    result_rationale: >\n      Per-type splitting 完全消除 type confusion（confusion=0，因为每 batch 只有一个 type）\n      但代价巨大：\n      (1) Cross-type context 完全丧失——模型无法通过排除其他类型来确认当前类型，\n      导致大量 false negatives（omission 4500 vs single-pass 2850）；\n      (2) 每个 batch 的 type 描述缺乏对比上下文，模型倾向于 over-predict（每个 batch\n      里任何看起来沾边的 span 都被标注），但因为只有一个 type 所以 precision 不高；\n      (3) 66 个 API calls 的延迟不可接受（45 min vs 4 min single-pass）；\n      (4) F1=0.395 低于 single-pass 和 SDGD-zero——这是\"过度分解\"的直接证据。\n      这个结果对论文至关重要：证明 naive decomposition (UniNER-style) 不是答案，\n      confusability-AWARE grouping（而非简单拆分）才是正确方向。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Decomposition Strategy Spectrum\"\n        content: |\n          | Strategy     | k  | F1    | Confusion | Omission | Latency (min) |\n          |-------------|-----|-------|-----------|----------|---------------|\n          | Single-pass | 1   | 0.414 | 2434      | 2850     | 4             |\n          | SDGD-zero   | 8   | 0.425 | 1850      | 3200     | 12            |\n          | Random      | 8   | 0.418 | 2150      | 3100     | 12            |\n          | Per-type    | 66  | 0.395 | 0         | 4500     | 45            |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Trade-off curve: F1 vs number of batches k, showing inverted-U peaking at k≈8-12. Per-type (k=66) falls off sharply.\"\n      - \"Stacked error bar: confusion + omission across strategies, showing the substitution↓/omission↑ tradeoff spectrum.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Per-type splitting 是 decomposition spectrum 的极端端点，其 F1 下降证明\n      cross-type context 有正面价值——LLM 需要看到相关类型才能做出正确区分。\n      SDGD 的价值在于找到 optimal k 使得 confusability reduction 和 context preservation\n      之间取得平衡。即使 SDGD-zero 增益不显著，它至少不损害性能（unlike per-type），\n      这本身就是有意义的 design insight。\n\n  - name: \"SCS vs Empirical Confusion Validation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-015\"\n    description: >\n      Spearman/Kendall correlation between embedding SCS 和 calibration 实测 confusion matrix。\n      验证 embedding proxy 的实用性上界。\n    expected_results:\n      fewnerd_qwen3:\n        spearman_rho: 0.35\n        kendall_tau: 0.25\n        p_value: 2.0e-08\n        n_pairs_with_confusion: 285\n      fewnerd_minilm:\n        spearman_rho: 0.22\n        kendall_tau: 0.16\n        p_value: 0.0003\n        n_pairs_with_confusion: 285\n      top10_overlap_qwen3: 0.50\n      top10_overlap_minilm: 0.30\n      rank_agreement_top50_qwen3: 0.42\n    result_rationale: >\n      Embedding SCS 与 empirical confusion 的相关性中等（ρ≈0.35 for Qwen3），原因是：\n      (1) Embedding 相似性捕获了语义距离但 LLM confusion 还受到：\n         - type name 的词汇重叠（\"person-artist\" vs \"person-politician\" 共享前缀）\n         - pretraining data 中类型的 co-occurrence 频率\n         - prompt 格式对不同类型名的 tokenization 差异\n      这些因素不反映在 embedding SCS 中；\n      (2) Qwen3 SCS > MiniLM SCS（ρ=0.35 vs 0.22）因为 Qwen3 是 extraction model\n      本身的 embedding，更接近模型内部的 type representation；\n      (3) Top-10 overlap 50%（Qwen3）意味着一半的最高混淆 pairs 被 embedding 正确识别，\n      但另一半被遗漏——这解释了为什么 SDGD-zero 效果有限而 SDGD-cal 更好。\n      这个结果为 embedding 选择提供了 principled guidance：\n      如果可以用 extraction model 自身的 embedding，优先使用；否则用 SDGD-cal。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: SCS vs Empirical Confusion Correlation\"\n        content: |\n          | Embedding | Spearman ρ | Kendall τ | Top-10 Overlap | n pairs |\n          |-----------|-----------|-----------|----------------|---------|\n          | Qwen3     | 0.35      | 0.25      | 50%            | 285     |\n          | MiniLM    | 0.22      | 0.16      | 30%            | 285     |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scatter: Qwen3 SCS vs empirical confusion rate (log scale), with marginal histograms showing SCS concentration.\"\n      - \"Precision-at-k curve: fraction of top-k SCS pairs that are in top-k empirical confusion pairs, for k=5,10,20,50.\"\n    analysis: >\n      SCS 是 reasonable proxy（ρ=0.35, 显著）但远非 perfect predictor（ρ<0.5）。\n      这解释了 SDGD-zero 与 SDGD-cal 的 performance gap，并为\"何时用哪种 SDGD 变体\"\n      提供了 decision criterion：embedding SCS 适合 quick-and-dirty decomposition，\n      empirical calibration 适合 high-stakes applications。\n      论文中作为 2×3 ablation 的 quantitative backing。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":17842,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":17842},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ae22442b-8538-43ef-9b60-9e46bd12db0d","uuid":"d2bb7cc1-0f22-49bf-b5f0-f8a1fa5a0db3"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":412532,"duration_api_ms":413915,"num_turns":1,"result":"```yaml\ntier: median\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  论文重心 80:20（分析:方法）。三层贡献：(1) pairwise confusability 跨 NER/RE/ED 三任务、Qwen3+LLaMA 双模型成立，\n  (2) multi-channel degradation model（count→omission, confusability→substitution）+ 错误分类学，\n  (3) centrality confound 方法论发现 + 2×3 embedding ablation practitioner guidance。\n  SDGD-zero 保留为 proof-of-concept 但 ΔF1 不显著（[-2,+2]pp），Claim 3 改写为\n  \"SDGD 框架示范 pairwise confusability 可直接指导 schema decomposition，SDGD-cal 预期有更大空间\"。\n  EMNLP Main 可冲（对标 Lost in the Middle），Findings 作后备。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"MAVEN Full Confusability Study\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-004\"\n    description: >\n      MAVEN 168 event类型，count curve + within-count BCS correlation + pairwise/per-type分析。\n      跨任务验证（NER→ED），同域语义密集 schema 的 confusability 行为。\n    expected_results:\n      count_curve_relaxed_f1:\n        count_1: 0.106\n        count_6: 0.103\n        count_12: 0.146\n        count_22: 0.185\n        count_44: 0.247\n        count_64: 0.245\n        count_168: 0.220\n      count_curve_exact_f1:\n        count_1: 0.009\n        count_6: 0.003\n        count_12: 0.008\n        count_22: 0.013\n        count_44: 0.018\n        count_64: 0.013\n      pairwise_minilm:\n        pearson_r: 0.115\n        pearson_p: 2.0e-34\n        n_pairs: 11026\n        spearman_rho: 0.098\n        spearman_p: 1.5e-24\n      pairwise_qwen3:\n        pearson_r: -0.007\n        pearson_p: 0.41\n        verdict: \"NOT_SIGNIFICANT\"\n      per_type_qwen3:\n        spearman_rho: 0.189\n        spearman_p: 0.021\n        direction: \"POSITIVE (centrality confound)\"\n      per_type_minilm:\n        spearman_rho: 0.208\n        spearman_p: 0.011\n        direction: \"POSITIVE (centrality confound)\"\n      within_count_bcs_relaxed_f1:\n        count_6_r: 0.12\n        count_6_p: 0.18\n        count_12_r: 0.09\n        count_12_p: 0.28\n        verdict: \"FAIL — batch-level BCS confounded by centrality\"\n      confusion_rate_ratio_extreme:\n        count_6: 7.5\n        count_12: 5.2\n    result_rationale: >\n      MAVEN 168 类型全部来自 FrameNet 同域层级，语义空间高度同质（scs_mean=0.216，\n      scs_std=0.103），导致两个层面行为分离：\n      (1) Pairwise MiniLM 成立（r≈0.12）——因为 MiniLM 对细粒度事件类型对（如 Destroying↔Damaging）\n      的相对差异敏感，pair-level 分析不受聚合效应影响；\n      (2) Pairwise Qwen3 不显著——Qwen3 extraction-aligned embedding 在同域 schema 中\n      将语义相近类型压缩到近乎相同的向量，丧失区分力；\n      (3) Per-type 两种 embedding 均为正向 ρ≈+0.19/+0.21——这是 centrality confound：\n      在同质 schema 中 mean BCS 高的类型恰好是语义中心、高频类型，LLM 对其提取效果好。\n      这不是分析失败，而是方法论贡献——识别出\"per-type 聚合在何时失效\"的具体机制。\n      Within-count batch-level 相关不显著，因为 batch-level BCS 范围被 schema 同质性压缩\n      （0.87-0.94），区分度不足。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: MAVEN Count Curve (Relaxed F1)\"\n        content: |\n          | Count | Relaxed F1 | Exact F1 | Recall | Precision |\n          |-------|-----------|----------|--------|-----------|\n          | 1     | 0.106     | 0.009    | 0.142  | 0.083     |\n          | 6     | 0.103     | 0.003    | 0.130  | 0.085     |\n          | 12    | 0.146     | 0.008    | 0.172  | 0.127     |\n          | 22    | 0.185     | 0.013    | 0.210  | 0.165     |\n          | 44    | 0.247     | 0.018    | 0.268  | 0.229     |\n          | 64    | 0.245     | 0.013    | 0.255  | 0.236     |\n      - name: \"Table: MAVEN Pairwise & Per-type Analysis (2×2 Embedding Matrix)\"\n        content: |\n          | Level     | Qwen3          | MiniLM          |\n          |-----------|----------------|-----------------|\n          | Pairwise  | r=-0.007 (ns)  | r=+0.115 ✓      |\n          | Per-type  | ρ=+0.189 ✗     | ρ=+0.208 ✗      |\n          Note: ✓=supports confusability hypothesis, ✗=centrality confound direction\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scatter plot: MiniLM pairwise SCS vs confusion count (11K pairs), with regression line r=0.115. Long tail of high-SCS pairs with elevated confusion.\"\n      - \"Bar chart: per-type mean BCS quartiles vs relaxed F1, showing positive trend (centrality confound). Annotated with frequency distribution per quartile.\"\n      - \"Heatmap: top-20 confused event type pairs, colored by MiniLM SCS. Diagonal stripe pattern showing FrameNet siblings.\"\n    analysis: >\n      MAVEN 为 pairwise confusability 提供跨任务复现（NER→ED），同时暴露 per-type 聚合的\n      centrality confound 机制。MiniLM pairwise r=0.115 与 Few-NERD r=0.156 量级一致，\n      但 Qwen3 在同域 schema 上失效，证实\"embedding 选择影响信号检测\"的结论。\n      Per-type 正向 ρ 构成独立方法论贡献：当 schema 语义同质时，mean BCS 不再是\n      confusability 的有效聚合指标，需回退到 pairwise level。\n\n  - name: \"DocRED Confusability Scaling Test\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-005\"\n    description: >\n      DocRED 96 relation types，count curve + BCS correlation。\n      文档级 RE 的 scaling stress test，验证 confusability 信号在更复杂抽取设置下是否成立。\n    expected_results:\n      count_curve_f1:\n        count_1: 0.18\n        count_6: 0.22\n        count_12: 0.25\n        count_24: 0.23\n        count_48: 0.19\n        count_96: 0.14\n      pairwise_qwen3:\n        pearson_r: 0.082\n        pearson_p: 0.008\n        n_pairs: 4560\n      pairwise_minilm:\n        pearson_r: 0.095\n        pearson_p: 0.001\n      per_type_qwen3:\n        spearman_rho: -0.165\n        spearman_p: 0.108\n      within_count_bcs_f1:\n        count_12_r: 0.18\n        count_12_p: 0.12\n        count_24_r: 0.25\n        count_24_p: 0.065\n    result_rationale: >\n      DocRED 是文档级 RE，96 relation types 跨越多域（人物、地理、组织等），\n      语义异质性介于 Few-NERD（跨域 NER）和 MAVEN（同域 ED）之间。\n      Pairwise 信号可检测（r≈0.08-0.10）但弱于 Few-NERD（r=0.156），原因是：\n      (1) 文档级 RE 噪声更大——同一文档多个 relation 共现，confusion 来源更复杂；\n      (2) relation type 的语义相似性比 entity type 更抽象（\"country of citizenship\" vs\n      \"place of birth\" 的 embedding 距离不完全反映 LLM 的实际混淆模式）；\n      (3) DocRED 的 distant supervision 标注本身有噪声，增加 metric variance。\n      Per-type 方向一致（负 ρ）但因 n=96 types + 噪声，未达显著。\n      作为 P1 实验，主要贡献是\"第四个数据点\"但非必须——三任务已足够。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: DocRED Count Curve\"\n        content: |\n          | Count | F1    | Recall | Precision |\n          |-------|-------|--------|-----------|\n          | 1     | 0.180 | 0.280  | 0.133     |\n          | 6     | 0.220 | 0.290  | 0.178     |\n          | 12    | 0.250 | 0.275  | 0.229     |\n          | 24    | 0.230 | 0.240  | 0.221     |\n          | 48    | 0.190 | 0.195  | 0.185     |\n          | 96    | 0.140 | 0.135  | 0.146     |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"DocRED count curve overlay with Few-NERD (normalized F1), showing both exhibit inverted-U but DocRED peaks earlier (count_12 vs count_44).\"\n    analysis: >\n      DocRED 提供第四个数据点但效应量衰减。如果时间紧张（ARR deadline 10 天），\n      可降级为 appendix 或完全跳过——Few-NERD + FewRel + MAVEN 已覆盖 NER/RE/ED 三任务。\n\n  - name: \"Count × Confusability Interaction Effect\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-006\"\n    description: >\n      2×2 factorial：{low count (6), high count (22)} × {low BCS, high BCS}，Few-NERD。\n      检验 count 和 confusability 的交互是加性还是乘性。\n    expected_results:\n      cell_f1:\n        low_count_low_bcs: 0.355\n        low_count_high_bcs: 0.305\n        high_count_low_bcs: 0.295\n        high_count_high_bcs: 0.230\n      main_effect_count:\n        delta_f1_pp: -6.3\n        f_stat: 8.2\n        p_value: 0.007\n      main_effect_bcs:\n        delta_f1_pp: -5.8\n        f_stat: 6.5\n        p_value: 0.015\n      interaction:\n        f_stat: 1.4\n        p_value: 0.24\n        effect_size_eta2: 0.03\n      model_comparison:\n        additive_R2: 0.38\n        multiplicative_R2: 0.39\n    result_rationale: >\n      Count 和 confusability 通过不同通道降解性能：count 导致 recall 下降（omission），\n      confusability 导致 precision 下降（substitution）。这两个通道大致正交——\n      增加 count 不会显著放大 confusability 的效应，反之亦然。\n      Interaction term 不显著（p≈0.24）的原因是：(1) 两通道作用于不同错误类型，\n      物理上近似独立；(2) 2×2 设计只有 ~20 batches/cell，检测交互效应的统计功效有限。\n      Additive model 已解释 ~38% 方差，interaction 仅贡献 1%。\n      这实际上支持 multi-channel model 的核心主张——count 和 confusability 可独立处理。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: 2×2 Factorial Results\"\n        content: |\n          |                | Low BCS  | High BCS | Marginal |\n          |----------------|----------|----------|----------|\n          | Low count (6)  | 0.355    | 0.305    | 0.330    |\n          | High count (22)| 0.295    | 0.230    | 0.263    |\n          | Marginal       | 0.325    | 0.268    |          |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Interaction plot: two roughly parallel lines (low BCS, high BCS) across count levels, illustrating additive (not synergistic) effect.\"\n    analysis: >\n      加性模型优于乘性模型但 margin 很小。关键 takeaway 是\"two independent knobs\"——\n      从业者可以分别优化 batch size（控制 count 通道）和 batch composition（控制 confusability 通道），\n      无需考虑复杂交互。这是 practitioner guidance 的基础。\n\n  - name: \"Systematic Error Taxonomy\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-007\"\n    description: >\n      跨 BCS bins 的 FP 系统分类：type_substitution / boundary_error / omission / hallucination。\n      为 multi-channel model 提供机制证据。\n    expected_results:\n      error_distribution_high_bcs:\n        type_substitution_pct: 62\n        boundary_error_pct: 14\n        omission_pct: 18\n        hallucination_pct: 6\n      error_distribution_low_bcs:\n        type_substitution_pct: 28\n        boundary_error_pct: 22\n        omission_pct: 42\n        hallucination_pct: 8\n      error_distribution_medium_bcs:\n        type_substitution_pct: 45\n        boundary_error_pct: 18\n        omission_pct: 30\n        hallucination_pct: 7\n      substitution_ratio_high_vs_low: 2.2\n      omission_ratio_low_vs_high: 2.3\n      substitution_trend_with_count:\n        count_6: 0.35\n        count_12: 0.48\n        count_22: 0.55\n      omission_trend_with_count:\n        count_6: 0.28\n        count_12: 0.32\n        count_22: 0.38\n    result_rationale: >\n      Error taxonomy 是 multi-channel model 的直接机制验证。\n      High-BCS batches 中 type_substitution 占主导（~62%）因为语义相似类型共现时\n      LLM 识别了正确的 span 但选错了类型标签——这正是 confusability channel 的定义。\n      Low-BCS batches 中 omission 占主导（~42%）因为虽然类型不相似但数量多，\n      LLM 的 attention 被分散，更多实体被完全遗漏——这是 count channel。\n      Substitution 随 count 增加（0.35→0.55）因为更多类型意味着更多潜在混淆对。\n      Omission 也随 count 增加（0.28→0.38）因为 attention dilution 加剧。\n      两种错误都对 count 有响应，但 confusability 只放大 substitution，不影响 omission——\n      这是两通道正交性的直接证据。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Error Distribution by BCS Bin\"\n        content: |\n          | Error Type       | Low BCS | Med BCS | High BCS |\n          |------------------|---------|---------|----------|\n          | Type Substitution| 28%     | 45%     | 62%      |\n          | Boundary Error   | 22%     | 18%     | 14%      |\n          | Omission         | 42%     | 30%     | 18%      |\n          | Hallucination    | 8%      | 7%      | 6%       |\n      - name: \"Table: Error Rates by Count Level (All BCS)\"\n        content: |\n          | Error Type       | Count 6 | Count 12 | Count 22 |\n          |------------------|---------|----------|----------|\n          | Substitution Rate| 0.035   | 0.048    | 0.055    |\n          | Omission Rate    | 0.028   | 0.032    | 0.038    |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Stacked bar chart: error type composition across 5 BCS quintiles, showing substitution/omission crossover at BCS≈0.82.\"\n      - \"Dual-axis line chart: substitution rate (left axis) and omission rate (right axis) vs count, both increasing but substitution steeper.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Error taxonomy 将 \"confusability degrades extraction\" 的抽象主张具象化为可操作的诊断框架：\n      看到 high substitution rate → confusability 问题 → SDGD-style decomposition；\n      看到 high omission rate → count 问题 → reduce batch size。\n      这本身是论文的独立贡献，特别是在 Claim 3 (SDGD gains) 不显著的 median 档下，\n      错误分类学提供了\"分析即贡献\"的具体证据。\n\n  - name: \"LLaMA-3.3-70B Multi-Model Validation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-012\"\n    description: >\n      LLaMA-3.3-70B-Instruct 复现 exp-002 协议。\n      验证 confusability 信号的模型无关性——是 schema 属性而非模型特异行为。\n    expected_results:\n      fewnerd_pairwise:\n        pearson_r: 0.098\n        pearson_p: 3.2e-05\n        n_pairs: 1953\n        spearman_rho: 0.105\n        spearman_p: 8.7e-06\n        nonzero_spearman_rho: 0.195\n        nonzero_spearman_p: 0.0004\n      fewnerd_per_type:\n        spearman_rho: -0.215\n        spearman_p: 0.089\n        partial_r_ctrl_logfreq: -0.155\n        partial_p: 0.225\n      count_curve_f1:\n        count_1: 0.285\n        count_6: 0.270\n        count_12: 0.305\n        count_22: 0.265\n        count_44: 0.380\n        count_64: 0.355\n      confusion_rate_ratio_extreme:\n        count_6: 12.5\n        count_12: 6.8\n      batch_level_f1_vs_bcs:\n        count_12_r: 0.38\n        count_12_p: 0.045\n    result_rationale: >\n      LLaMA-3.3-70B 复现 pairwise 信号（r≈0.10, p<0.001）但效应量小于 Qwen3（r=0.156），\n      原因是：\n      (1) LLaMA 和 Qwen3 架构不同（LLaMA 使用 GQA vs Qwen3 使用 GQA+SWA），\n      对 prompt 中类型列表的 attention 分配模式不同，导致 confusability 的表现形式有差异；\n      (2) LLaMA-70B 参数量更大（70B vs 32B），可能对 confusable types 有更强的区分能力，\n      从而压缩效应量；\n      (3) 但 pairwise 信号方向一致且显著——confusability 是 schema 结构属性，\n      不同模型都会受影响，只是程度不同。\n      Per-type ρ=-0.215 方向一致但 p=0.089 未达 0.05——这在 median 档预期范围内\n      （cross_model_significant: [1,2]），pairwise 显著已足够支撑 multi-model claim。\n      Overall F1 水平比 Qwen3 低 5-10%，可能因 LLaMA 的 NER few-shot 能力略弱。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Cross-Model Pairwise Comparison\"\n        content: |\n          | Metric              | Qwen3-32B   | LLaMA-3.3-70B |\n          |---------------------|-------------|---------------|\n          | Pairwise r          | 0.156       | 0.098         |\n          | Pairwise p          | 4.6e-12     | 3.2e-05       |\n          | Per-type ρ          | -0.293*     | -0.215        |\n          | Confusion ratio (6) | 27.5x       | 12.5x         |\n          | Confusion ratio (12)| 9.9x        | 6.8x          |\n          * p<0.05\n      - name: \"Table: LLaMA Count Curve\"\n        content: |\n          | Count | F1    | Recall | Precision |\n          |-------|-------|--------|-----------|\n          | 1     | 0.285 | 0.580  | 0.190     |\n          | 6     | 0.270 | 0.420  | 0.200     |\n          | 12    | 0.305 | 0.310  | 0.300     |\n          | 22    | 0.265 | 0.255  | 0.275     |\n          | 44    | 0.380 | 0.365  | 0.396     |\n          | 64    | 0.355 | 0.280  | 0.485     |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Overlay scatter: Qwen3 vs LLaMA pairwise SCS-confusion, same axes. Both positive slopes, LLaMA shallower.\"\n      - \"Side-by-side confusion heatmaps (top-20 pairs): substantial overlap in confused pairs between models.\"\n    analysis: >\n      LLaMA 在 pairwise level 显著复现信号（r≥0.08, p<0.05），满足 median 档\n      cross_model_significant ≥1 的阈值。Per-type 未达显著但方向一致。\n      效应量差异本身是有意义的发现——更大的模型可能对 confusability 更鲁棒，\n      暗示 confusability 降解是 training-free setting 的固有挑战，可通过 scaling 部分缓解但不消除。\n      论文中报告为\"cross-model replication with attenuated but significant effect\"。\n\n  - name: \"SDGD-zero on Few-NERD\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-008\"\n    description: >\n      Confusability-minimizing batch composition：embedding SCS 阈值化 → confusability graph →\n      graph coloring → batches。对比 single-pass full-schema baseline。\n    expected_results:\n      sdgd_zero_config:\n        embedding: \"qwen3\"\n        threshold: 0.85\n        n_batches: 8\n        avg_batch_size: 8.25\n        coloring_algorithm: \"greedy_dsatur\"\n      sdgd_zero_f1: 0.425\n      singlepass_f1: 0.414\n      delta_f1_pp: 1.1\n      delta_f1_ci_95: [-1.5, 3.7]\n      p_value_paired_t: 0.18\n      significant: false\n      sdgd_zero_recall: 0.335\n      sdgd_zero_precision: 0.580\n      singlepass_recall: 0.304\n      singlepass_precision: 0.648\n      type_confusion_errors:\n        sdgd_zero: 1850\n        singlepass: 2434\n        reduction_pct: 24\n      omission_errors:\n        sdgd_zero: 3200\n        singlepass: 2850\n        increase_pct: 12\n      api_calls: 8\n      wall_clock_ratio: 3.2\n    result_rationale: >\n      SDGD-zero 在 median 档下 ΔF1≈+1.1pp，置信区间跨零，不显著。核心权衡：\n      (1) Confusability 降低的收益——分离 confusable types（如 person-other 和 person-politician\n      不再共现于同一 batch），type confusion errors 减少 ~24%，precision 改善；\n      (2) 跨类型上下文丢失的代价——单 batch 只看到 ~8 个类型而非全部 66 个，\n      LLM 无法利用\"这不是 X 所以应该是 Y\"的排除推理，omission errors 增加 ~12%；\n      (3) 这两个效应在 F1 层面大致抵消。Precision 提升（0.648→0.580 actually下降...\n      不对，让我修正）——SDGD-zero 的 recall 高于 single-pass（0.335>0.304）因为\n      smaller batches 意味着更少的 attention dilution，但 precision 降低因为\n      smaller batches 使模型缺少同 batch 内的对比信号。\n      净效应：recall 提升 + precision 下降 → F1 微小提升但不显著。\n      这正是 median 档的核心判断——decomposition 是可行的框架但不是 silver bullet。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: SDGD-zero vs Single-pass on Few-NERD (66 types)\"\n        content: |\n          | Method      | F1    | Recall | Precision | Type Confusion | Omission | API Calls |\n          |-------------|-------|--------|-----------|----------------|----------|-----------|\n          | Single-pass | 0.414 | 0.304  | 0.648     | 2434           | 2850     | 1         |\n          | SDGD-zero   | 0.425 | 0.335  | 0.580     | 1850           | 3200     | 8         |\n          | Δ           | +1.1  | +3.1   | -6.8      | -24%           | +12%     | +7        |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Paired bar chart: error type breakdown for single-pass vs SDGD-zero, showing substitution↓ / omission↑ tradeoff.\"\n      - \"Scatter: per-batch F1 vs batch mean BCS for SDGD-zero batches, showing SDGD batches cluster at low BCS.\"\n    analysis: >\n      SDGD-zero 的价值不在于 F1 增益（不显著），而在于：\n      (1) 验证 pairwise confusability 可直接转化为 actionable decomposition；\n      (2) 错误 profile 的定向转移证实 multi-channel model——confusability channel 可关闭（减 24% substitution），\n      但代价是轻度激活 count channel（增 12% omission）；\n      (3) 为 SDGD-cal 提供 baseline——如果用 empirical confusion 替代 embedding proxy，\n      graph 更准确，预期收益更大。\n\n  - name: \"SDGD-zero on MAVEN\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-009\"\n    description: >\n      SDGD-zero 在 MAVEN 168 event types 上的跨任务验证。\n      同域高密度 schema 对 graph coloring 的挑战。\n    expected_results:\n      sdgd_zero_config:\n        embedding: \"minilm\"\n        threshold: 0.35\n        n_batches: 14\n        avg_batch_size: 12\n      sdgd_zero_relaxed_f1: 0.240\n      singlepass_relaxed_f1: 0.245\n      random_batching_relaxed_f1: 0.235\n      delta_vs_singlepass_pp: -0.5\n      delta_vs_random_pp: 0.5\n      significant: false\n      sdgd_zero_exact_f1: 0.015\n      singlepass_exact_f1: 0.013\n      api_calls: 14\n    result_rationale: >\n      MAVEN 的同域同质 schema 对 SDGD-zero 极具挑战：\n      (1) SCS 分布集中（mean=0.216, std=0.103），大部分 pair 相似度在 0.1-0.35 范围，\n      用阈值 0.35 切分后 confusability graph 边数较少，graph coloring 产生的 batches\n      与 random batching 差异不大；\n      (2) 即使成功分离了高 SCS pairs（119 pairs > 0.5），这些 pairs 分布在 168 个 types\n      中仅占 0.85%，对整体 F1 影响微小；\n      (3) Exact F1 极低（<0.02）使得任何方法差异都淹没在 boundary matching 噪声中，\n      relaxed F1 是唯一可比指标；\n      (4) SDGD-zero 微弱优于 random batching（+0.5pp），但不优于 single-pass（-0.5pp），\n      因为 MAVEN 的 context 更重要——event detection 依赖同一句中多种事件类型的对比。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: SDGD-zero vs Baselines on MAVEN (168 types)\"\n        content: |\n          | Method          | Relaxed F1 | Exact F1 | API Calls |\n          |-----------------|-----------|----------|-----------|\n          | Single-pass     | 0.245     | 0.013    | 1         |\n          | Random (k=14)   | 0.235     | 0.012    | 14        |\n          | SDGD-zero       | 0.240     | 0.015    | 14        |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"MAVEN confusability graph visualization: near-complete subgraph structure, illustrating why graph coloring fails to find clean separations.\"\n    analysis: >\n      MAVEN 上 SDGD-zero ≈ single-pass 进一步支持 median 档叙事：\n      SDGD 是正确的框架但 -zero 变体在高密度 schema 上能力有限。\n      这也解释了为什么 embedding-based proxy 不够——需要 empirical confusion data (SDGD-cal)\n      才能在同域 schema 上有效操作。\n\n  - name: \"SDGD-cal on Few-NERD\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-010\"\n    description: >\n      用 5-10 calibration examples 的 empirical confusion matrix 替代 embedding SCS 构建 confusability graph。\n      检验 calibration 数据能否弥补 embedding proxy 的不足。\n    expected_results:\n      calibration_config:\n        n_calibration_examples: 8\n        calibration_api_calls: 528\n        total_api_calls: 536\n      sdgd_cal_f1: 0.440\n      sdgd_zero_f1: 0.425\n      singlepass_f1: 0.414\n      delta_cal_vs_zero_pp: 1.5\n      delta_cal_vs_singlepass_pp: 2.6\n      delta_cal_vs_singlepass_ci_95: [-0.8, 6.0]\n      p_value_vs_singlepass: 0.09\n      significant_vs_singlepass: false\n      type_confusion_reduction_vs_singlepass_pct: 35\n      calibration_confusion_vs_scs_spearman: 0.32\n    result_rationale: >\n      SDGD-cal 相比 SDGD-zero 提升 ~1.5pp，原因是 empirical confusion 直接捕获\n      模型特异的混淆模式（如 Qwen3 特别容易混淆 building-library ↔ building-hotel\n      但 embedding 距离中等的 pair），绕过了 embedding proxy 的噪声。\n      但 +2.6pp vs single-pass 仍不显著（p≈0.09），因为：\n      (1) 8 个 calibration examples 的 confusion matrix 高方差——很多 type pairs\n      在 8 个样本中从未共现，confusion 为 0 但真实 confusability 非零；\n      (2) 从 calibration 到 test set 的 confusion 分布偏移——calibration examples\n      的 type 分布未必代表 test set；\n      (3) context loss 问题仍在——SDGD-cal 只改善了 confusability graph 的质量，\n      不改变 decomposition 本身的 context-loss tradeoff。\n      这个结果在 median 档下留出\"SDGD-cal 有空间\"的 narrative——\n      更多 calibration data 或更好的 calibration protocol 预期可以继续提升。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: SDGD Variant Comparison on Few-NERD\"\n        content: |\n          | Method      | F1    | ΔF1 vs SP | Type Confusion ↓ | API Calls |\n          |-------------|-------|-----------|------------------|-----------|\n          | Single-pass | 0.414 | —         | —                | 1         |\n          | SDGD-zero   | 0.425 | +1.1      | -24%             | 8         |\n          | SDGD-cal    | 0.440 | +2.6      | -35%             | 536       |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Line chart: F1 improvement trajectory from single-pass → SDGD-zero → SDGD-cal, with error bars. Upward trend but CIs overlap.\"\n      - \"Confusion matrix diff: empirical (calibration) vs embedding-predicted, highlighting discrepancies.\"\n    analysis: >\n      SDGD-cal 展示 confusability-aware decomposition 的 ceiling 更高，\n      但 8-example calibration 尚不足以稳定地达到。论文可报告为\"SDGD-cal 提供方向，\n      充分 calibration 数据下预期更大收益，但当前 training-free 设定下的 calibration 成本\n      与收益比尚需优化\"。作为 SDGD-cal 的存在证明而非 headline 结果。\n\n  - name: \"SDGD-cal on MAVEN\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-011\"\n    description: >\n      SDGD-cal 在 MAVEN 168 event types 上运行。\n      测试 empirical confusion 能否克服 MAVEN 上 embedding proxy 失效的问题。\n    expected_results:\n      sdgd_cal_relaxed_f1: 0.258\n      sdgd_zero_relaxed_f1: 0.240\n      singlepass_relaxed_f1: 0.245\n      delta_cal_vs_singlepass_pp: 1.3\n      delta_cal_vs_zero_pp: 1.8\n      significant: false\n      calibration_api_calls: 1344\n      total_api_calls: 1358\n    result_rationale: >\n      MAVEN 上 SDGD-cal 比 SDGD-zero 收益更大（+1.8pp vs +0.5pp on Few-NERD），\n      因为 MAVEN 正是 embedding proxy 失效的数据集（Qwen3 pairwise r=-0.007）。\n      Empirical confusion 绕过了 embedding 的限制，直接用模型行为构建 graph。\n      但绝对增益仍有限（+1.3pp vs single-pass），因为：\n      (1) 168 types 的 calibration matrix 极其稀疏——168×167/2=14028 pairs 中，\n      8 个 calibration samples 能覆盖的 pair 比例很低；\n      (2) MAVEN 的 exact F1 极低，relaxed F1 的 variance 大，信噪比低；\n      (3) 1344 API calls 的 calibration 成本在实用性上存疑。\n      这支持了\"SDGD-cal 在 embedding 失效场景下价值更大\"的论点，\n      也说明了\"calibration 效率是未来工作方向\"。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: SDGD-cal vs Baselines on MAVEN\"\n        content: |\n          | Method      | Relaxed F1 | Δ vs SP  | API Calls |\n          |-------------|-----------|----------|-----------|\n          | Single-pass | 0.245     | —        | 1         |\n          | SDGD-zero   | 0.240     | -0.5     | 14        |\n          | SDGD-cal    | 0.258     | +1.3     | 1358      |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Grouped bar chart: SDGD-zero vs SDGD-cal improvement over single-pass, Few-NERD vs MAVEN. MAVEN shows larger cal-zero gap.\"\n    analysis: >\n      MAVEN 上 SDGD-cal > SDGD-zero 的差距（1.8pp）大于 Few-NERD（1.5pp），\n      验证了\"当 embedding proxy 失效时 empirical calibration 价值更高\"的预测。\n      但绝对增益仍不显著，reinforces median-tier narrative。\n\n  - name: \"Random Batching Ablation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-013\"\n    description: >\n      Random batching（与 SDGD 同 k，随机分组）ablation。\n      隔离 confusability-aware grouping 的贡献 vs 纯 batch count reduction。\n    expected_results:\n      random_batching_f1: 0.418\n      sdgd_zero_f1: 0.425\n      singlepass_f1: 0.414\n      delta_sdgd_vs_random_pp: 0.7\n      delta_random_vs_singlepass_pp: 0.4\n      random_batching_recall: 0.325\n      random_batching_precision: 0.565\n      type_confusion_errors:\n        random: 2150\n        sdgd_zero: 1850\n        singlepass: 2434\n      n_random_seeds: 5\n      f1_std_across_seeds: 0.018\n    result_rationale: >\n      Random batching vs single-pass 仅 +0.4pp——count reduction 本身的收益很小，\n      因为 Few-NERD 66 types 分成 8 batches of ~8 types，每个 batch 仍然有足够的\n      type diversity 来产生 confusion。Random batching 的 confusion rate 高于 SDGD-zero\n      但低于 single-pass，因为随机分组偶然也会分开一些 confusable pairs。\n      SDGD-zero vs random 的差异（+0.7pp）代表了 confusability-aware grouping 的\n      增量贡献——统计上不显著但方向一致，5 seeds 的 F1 std=0.018 反映分组方案敏感性。\n      这个结果在 median 档下支持\"SDGD 的 confusability-aware grouping 有正面方向\n      但需要更好的 confusability 信号（如 SDGD-cal）才能变得显著\"的叙事。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Batching Strategy Ablation (Few-NERD, k=8)\"\n        content: |\n          | Strategy     | F1    | Recall | Prec  | TypeConfusion | Seeds |\n          |-------------|-------|--------|-------|---------------|-------|\n          | Single-pass | 0.414 | 0.304  | 0.648 | 2434          | 1     |\n          | Random      | 0.418 | 0.325  | 0.565 | 2150          | 5     |\n          | SDGD-zero   | 0.425 | 0.335  | 0.580 | 1850          | 1     |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Box plot: 5 random seeds' F1 distribution vs SDGD-zero (single point), SDGD-zero at or near upper end of random distribution.\"\n    analysis: >\n      SDGD-zero 位于 random batching 分布的上端但未显著超出——\n      这意味着 confusability-aware grouping 有 signal 但 magnitude 有限。\n      报告为\"SDGD directionality confirmed, magnitude requires stronger confusability signal\"。\n\n  - name: \"Per-type Splitting (UniNER-style) Ablation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-014\"\n    description: >\n      每个 type 一个 batch（k=66），UniNER 风格。\n      消融 decomposition 的上界和 cross-type context loss 效应。\n    expected_results:\n      per_type_f1: 0.395\n      sdgd_zero_f1: 0.425\n      singlepass_f1: 0.414\n      delta_per_type_vs_singlepass_pp: -1.9\n      delta_per_type_vs_sdgd_pp: -3.0\n      per_type_recall: 0.385\n      per_type_precision: 0.405\n      api_calls: 66\n      wall_clock_minutes: 45\n      sdgd_wall_clock_minutes: 12\n      singlepass_wall_clock_minutes: 4\n      type_confusion_errors: 0\n      omission_errors: 4500\n    result_rationale: >\n      Per-type splitting 完全消除 type confusion（confusion=0，因为每 batch 只有一个 type）\n      但代价巨大：\n      (1) Cross-type context 完全丧失——模型无法通过排除其他类型来确认当前类型，\n      导致大量 false negatives（omission 4500 vs single-pass 2850）；\n      (2) 每个 batch 的 type 描述缺乏对比上下文，模型倾向于 over-predict（每个 batch\n      里任何看起来沾边的 span 都被标注），但因为只有一个 type 所以 precision 不高；\n      (3) 66 个 API calls 的延迟不可接受（45 min vs 4 min single-pass）；\n      (4) F1=0.395 低于 single-pass 和 SDGD-zero——这是\"过度分解\"的直接证据。\n      这个结果对论文至关重要：证明 naive decomposition (UniNER-style) 不是答案，\n      confusability-AWARE grouping（而非简单拆分）才是正确方向。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Decomposition Strategy Spectrum\"\n        content: |\n          | Strategy     | k  | F1    | Confusion | Omission | Latency (min) |\n          |-------------|-----|-------|-----------|----------|---------------|\n          | Single-pass | 1   | 0.414 | 2434      | 2850     | 4             |\n          | SDGD-zero   | 8   | 0.425 | 1850      | 3200     | 12            |\n          | Random      | 8   | 0.418 | 2150      | 3100     | 12            |\n          | Per-type    | 66  | 0.395 | 0         | 4500     | 45            |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Trade-off curve: F1 vs number of batches k, showing inverted-U peaking at k≈8-12. Per-type (k=66) falls off sharply.\"\n      - \"Stacked error bar: confusion + omission across strategies, showing the substitution↓/omission↑ tradeoff spectrum.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Per-type splitting 是 decomposition spectrum 的极端端点，其 F1 下降证明\n      cross-type context 有正面价值——LLM 需要看到相关类型才能做出正确区分。\n      SDGD 的价值在于找到 optimal k 使得 confusability reduction 和 context preservation\n      之间取得平衡。即使 SDGD-zero 增益不显著，它至少不损害性能（unlike per-type），\n      这本身就是有意义的 design insight。\n\n  - name: \"SCS vs Empirical Confusion Validation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-015\"\n    description: >\n      Spearman/Kendall correlation between embedding SCS 和 calibration 实测 confusion matrix。\n      验证 embedding proxy 的实用性上界。\n    expected_results:\n      fewnerd_qwen3:\n        spearman_rho: 0.35\n        kendall_tau: 0.25\n        p_value: 2.0e-08\n        n_pairs_with_confusion: 285\n      fewnerd_minilm:\n        spearman_rho: 0.22\n        kendall_tau: 0.16\n        p_value: 0.0003\n        n_pairs_with_confusion: 285\n      top10_overlap_qwen3: 0.50\n      top10_overlap_minilm: 0.30\n      rank_agreement_top50_qwen3: 0.42\n    result_rationale: >\n      Embedding SCS 与 empirical confusion 的相关性中等（ρ≈0.35 for Qwen3），原因是：\n      (1) Embedding 相似性捕获了语义距离但 LLM confusion 还受到：\n         - type name 的词汇重叠（\"person-artist\" vs \"person-politician\" 共享前缀）\n         - pretraining data 中类型的 co-occurrence 频率\n         - prompt 格式对不同类型名的 tokenization 差异\n      这些因素不反映在 embedding SCS 中；\n      (2) Qwen3 SCS > MiniLM SCS（ρ=0.35 vs 0.22）因为 Qwen3 是 extraction model\n      本身的 embedding，更接近模型内部的 type representation；\n      (3) Top-10 overlap 50%（Qwen3）意味着一半的最高混淆 pairs 被 embedding 正确识别，\n      但另一半被遗漏——这解释了为什么 SDGD-zero 效果有限而 SDGD-cal 更好。\n      这个结果为 embedding 选择提供了 principled guidance：\n      如果可以用 extraction model 自身的 embedding，优先使用；否则用 SDGD-cal。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: SCS vs Empirical Confusion Correlation\"\n        content: |\n          | Embedding | Spearman ρ | Kendall τ | Top-10 Overlap | n pairs |\n          |-----------|-----------|-----------|----------------|---------|\n          | Qwen3     | 0.35      | 0.25      | 50%            | 285     |\n          | MiniLM    | 0.22      | 0.16      | 30%            | 285     |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scatter: Qwen3 SCS vs empirical confusion rate (log scale), with marginal histograms showing SCS concentration.\"\n      - \"Precision-at-k curve: fraction of top-k SCS pairs that are in top-k empirical confusion pairs, for k=5,10,20,50.\"\n    analysis: >\n      SCS 是 reasonable proxy（ρ=0.35, 显著）但远非 perfect predictor（ρ<0.5）。\n      这解释了 SDGD-zero 与 SDGD-cal 的 performance gap，并为\"何时用哪种 SDGD 变体\"\n      提供了 decision criterion：embedding SCS 适合 quick-and-dirty decomposition，\n      empirical calibration 适合 high-stakes applications。\n      论文中作为 2×3 ablation 的 quantitative backing。\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"ae22442b-8538-43ef-9b60-9e46bd12db0d","total_cost_usd":0.639252,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":17842,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"output_tokens":20355,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":17842,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":20355,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation_input_tokens":17842,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":17842},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":